This directory contains a real example of a message excripted
on an M4 Enigma and sent by Dönitz towards the end of WWII to
his U-boats.

The file 'Original' contains the full original message.

Decrypting the message goes as follows:

(1) First set the Enigma to the settings of that day by double
    clicking the 'Setup' file.

(2) Type the fist 8 characters of the original message.
    Alternatively drag the file 'Initial' into the Enigma
    window. This should reveal two identical groups of 4
    characters each. Set the wheels on the Enigma to this
    setting (ASTV).

(3) Now type the rest of the message, or drag the file
    'Message' into the Enigma window. The rest of the message
    should now be decripted.

Please note that it may still be difficult to read the resulting
message. First of all it's in German and secondly, all spaces
are replaced by an 'X'. Characters like 'ö' are expanded to 'oe'
as is common practice in German.

Please refer to chapter 10.4 of the Enigma HTML manual for a
full description of the context of this message.


